      "message": "this isn\u0027t threadsafe (not that it needs to be, but) w/ C++11, you can just do:\n\nstatic sp\u003cFastboot\u003e instance_ \u003d new Fastboot();\nreturn instace_;\n\nand it will get called the first time. However, it\u0027s more typical for these to return a new instance every time. If you do that (and make the client handle the singleton) I think it would be more consistent w/ the rest of the platform.\n\nYou could just use HIDL_FETCH_IFastboot for future compatibility. Up to you.",
